      "content": "that makes sense. so it's basically just an issue of instability during the cooling phase. i noticed that when the bloom happens, it almost looks like something is growing or \"sprouting\" out from under the surface of the chocolate rather than just being a layer on top. is there a reason the crystals look so much more \"active\" or chaotic when they bloom compared to a clean set?",
